{"name":"Apricot Jam","hex":"#eea771","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"apricot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A round sweet and juicy stone fruit, resembling peach or plum in taste, with a yellow-orange flesh, lightly fuzzy skin and a large seed inside.","The apricot tree, Prunus armeniaca."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale yellowish-orange colour, like that of an apricot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apricot"},{"term":"jam","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Jamaican Creole."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet mixture of fruit boiled with sugar and allowed to congeal. Often spread on bread or toast or used in jam tarts","A difficult situation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jam"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fruit preserves","blocks":[{"text":"Fruit preserves are preparations of fruits whose main preserving agent is sugar and sometimes acid, often stored in glass jars and used as a condiment or spread."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Fruits_jam_variants.jpg/330px-Fruits_jam_variants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit_preserves","wikidata":"Q74048276"},{"title":"Apricot","blocks":[{"text":"An apricot is a fruit, or the tree that bears the fruit, of several species in the genus Prunus. Usually an apricot is from the species Prunus armeniaca, but the fruits of the other species in Prunus sect. Armeniaca are also called apricots. In 2023, world production of apricots was 3.7 million tonnes, led by Turkey with 20% of the total."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Apricot_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Apricot_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apricot","wikidata":"Q3733836"},{"title":"Apricot (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Apricot is a light yellowish-orangish color that is similar to the color of apricots. However, it is paler than actual apricots."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apricot_(color)","wikidata":"Q1324818"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Ribotroshhashana.jpg/500px-Ribotroshhashana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Ribotroshhashana.jpg/1280px-Ribotroshhashana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Ribotroshhashana.jpg/500px-Ribotroshhashana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Five varieties of fruit preserves (clockwise from top): apple, quince, plum, squash, orange (in the center)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARibotroshhashana.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Colmar_%286710880299%29.jpg/500px-Colmar_%286710880299%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Colmar_%286710880299%29.jpg/1280px-Colmar_%286710880299%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Colmar_%286710880299%29.jpg/500px-Colmar_%286710880299%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jars of confiture and gelée for sale in Colmar, France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColmar_(6710880299).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Yujacha_%28yuja_tea%29.jpg/500px-Yujacha_%28yuja_tea%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Yujacha_%28yuja_tea%29.jp